{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And the magicians did so with their secret arts to bring forth the lice.</b> It mentions 'and they did so' because thus they struck the earth, and they pronounced the oath over the demons according to their custom in the other plagues, and this was in order to bring forth the lice, but they could not — and this demonstrates that what was mentioned above, 'and the magicians did so,' in the sign of the serpent and in the plague of blood, was all counterfeit action and all illusion; and one should not understand 'and they did so' as that they actually did so, and this verse testifies to this concerning them, for it says, ״ולא יכלו״ — 'and they could not.' And as for the fact that it mentioned them above by the name חרטומי מצרים ('the magicians of Egypt') and now mentions them by the name חרטומים without specification — it is possible to explain that since the magicians were great sages in the eyes of Egypt, Scripture mentioned them above twice with the definite article: in the sign of the serpent and in the plague of blood, namely, in the sign of the serpent it is written ״חרטומי מצרים בלהטיהם״, and in the plague of blood ״חרטומי מצרים בלטיהם״; and by this it declared their wisdom, which is the wisdom of sorcery and the wisdom of demons, and therefore it mentioned them twice with the definite article and with honor, for they were renowned and men of name in those arts. But afterward, in the plague of the frogs, their wisdom and their status were diminished in the eyes of Egypt, and they lost that title, and Scripture called them simply חרטומים, not חרטומי מצרים as at first, and this is what it says: ״ויעשו כן החרטומים בלטיהם ויעלו את הצפרדעים״. And then, in the plague of the lice, their wisdom was nullified and their status diminished yet more and more, when they were compelled against their will to acknowledge ״אצבע אלהים היא״ — they said, for it is a plague from HaShem, may He be exalted. He mentioned them with the loss of the title and with the loss of the ability, which is what it says: ״ויעשו כן החרטומים בלטיהם להוציא את הכנים ולא יכלו״ — החרטמים is written (defectively, without the ו). And from the plague of the lice onward they vanished from Scripture and are not mentioned again by the name חרטומי מצרים nor even חרטומים without specification (with the loss of the title and the loss of the ability), as it is written in the plague of the boils: ״ולא יכלו החרטומים לעמוד לפני משה״ — for they were ashamed and could not save themselves."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The parenthetical '(בחסרון השם וחסרון היכולת)' appears twice; translated literally each time. 'השבעת השדים' rendered as 'the oath over the demons,' i.e., the conjuration formula. The defective spelling החרטמים (without ו) refers to the plene form החרטומים."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:05.920492313Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}